4.29.m:
Bestowing radiance, bestowing strength, her sins uprooted by might;
Sinless, free from anguish, devoid of doubts,
Causing rain, rainwater [herself], rule [of law], her bonds severed;
Embodying vows, embodying wealth, destroyer of many obstacles,
Stream of wealth, earth, having variegated limbs, fire;
Victorious, the seed of the universe, Vāmadevī, giver of boons,
Resorting to righteousness, destroyer of poison, garlanded with waves of wisdom;
Auspicious, Bhogavatī, gracious, Bhavānī, creating living beings,
Supporter of beings, dispeller of fear, slayer of the poverty of devotees;
Granting worldly enjoyment and liberation, fearless, giving heaven and final release to devotees,
Bhāgīrathī, radiant, endowed with fortune and enjoyment, sustenance;
Beloved of Śiva, hating worldly existence, bestowing prosperity, adorned with ashes,
Knowing the thoughts of the three-eyed one, sovereign over the past, future, and present;
Quieter of deluded knowledge, shattering the pavilion of the cosmic egg,
Bestowing abundantly, easily attained through devotion, within the sight of the fortunate;
Crushing the host of calamities, bestowing the joy of food and drink,

To be sought by begging, mother of mendicants, embodying existence and non-existence;
Mandākinī, greatly delightful, mother, river of liberation,
Great dawn, full of sweetness, possessing great merit, causing joy;
Praised by sages, slayer of delusion, great tīrtha, flowing with honey,
Consort of Mādhava, proud, venerable, transcending the path of desires;
Giver of liberation, giver of intellect, foremost, resorted to by men of great fortune,
Having great speed, pure, adorned with great majesty;
Possessing great majesty, great one, with eyes restless like fish,
Filled with great compassion, possessing great prosperity, a great blue lotus;
Embodied maiden of liberation, adorned with jewels and rubies,
Attired in pearl ornaments, delighting mind and eye;
Destroyer of masses of great sins, occupying half the body of Mahādeva,
Garlanded with great waves, liberated, Mahādevī, Manonmanī;
Attainable by the rise of great merit, moonlight dispelling the darkness of illusion,
Great learning, great illusion, great intelligence, great panacea;
Wearing a garland, great means, adorned with great serpents,
Dispeller of great delusion, the most auspicious of great auspicious things;

Moving in the disc of the sun, Mahālakṣmī, free from pride;
Famous, giver of fame, fit, served by those disciplined in soul;
Bestower of yogic perfections, worthy of sacrifice, filled with the lord of sacrifice,
Ruler of sacrifices, giver of the fruit of sacrifice, worthy of worship, conferring renown;
Served by self-restrained ones, source of yoga, yoginī, giver of focused intellect,
Bestower of knowledge of yoga, disciplined, endowed with the eight-limbed yoga beginning with restraint;
Checking the movement of floods of sin, warding off the realm of Yama,
Calming transmigration, cutting away the names of torment;
Pure as the moon or snow, free from the conditions of the ages,
Revatī, causing pleasure, charming, full of gems, Ramā, Rati;
Object of love for the ocean, connoisseur, embodying aesthetic flavor,
Holding jewel palaces within, charming river;
Radiance of jewels, beloved of Rudra, destroying passion and hatred,
Ramā, beautiful woman, charming in form, life-giving medicine for the sick;
Creating delight, pleasant, charming, radiant, removing diseases,
Royal swan, rich in jewels, having lines of gleaming billows;
The very line of beauty, enemy of pain, angry at sickness,
Calming the affliction of beggars on the full moon, lovely, humming with bees;
